384011645,"_gp_fcf_yield":true,"_score_fcf_yield":100.0,"_gate_int_coverage":-5.406469760900141,"_gp_int_coverage":false,"_score_int_coverage":0.0,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":0.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.22967440046792748,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":90.7,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.20227895108017965,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":56.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.2312219878611872,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":-0.07794634636604514,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":2.227074840847974,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.4133929486486935,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.2865544424083129,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.10028392175937206,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":75.1,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.3340434436624862,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":-0.01115898271238366,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":38.8,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03427006904420009,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":49.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.11905723300075088,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.005586311021640664,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":90.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.02259,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":15.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Mativ Holdings, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, manufactures and sells specialty materials in the United States, Europe, the Asia Pacific, the Americas, and internationally. The company operates through two segments, Filtration & Advanced Materials and Sustainable & Adhesive Solutions. The Filtration & Advanced Materials manufactures and sells various engineered polymer, resin and fiber-based substrates, nets, films, adhesive tapes, and other nonwovens for transportation, water and air filtration, construction, healthcare, advertising and marketing, and consumer goods, as well as filtration media and components, advanced films, coating and converting solutions, and extruded mesh products. The Sustainable & Adhesive Solutions segment offers tapes, labels, and liners that includes substrates for tapes used in building and construction, infrastructure, DIY, athletic, and industrial applications; and substrates critical to protection and adhesive separation applications in the personal care, label, tape, industrial, graphic arts, composites, and medical categories, as well as performance labels and cable wrapping. This segment also provides paper and packaging products comprising premium printing and other specialty papers and packaging applications used for print collateral, advertising, direct mail, sustainable alternatives, product packaging, graphics, wallpaper, and education, as well as consumer office, stationery and craft papers to retailers, small business, personal use, and educational applications; and healthcare and other products, including wound care, consumer wellness, device fixation, medical packaging, as well as various other solutions and applications. The company was formerly known as Schweitzer-Mauduit International, Inc. and changed its name to Mativ Holdings, Inc. in July 2022. Mativ Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 1995 and is headquartered in Alpharetta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Shruti  Singhal | President, CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $397K ranks in the bottom quartile among Basic Materials peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $19K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Mativ Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $651M market cap on $2.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -3.1pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 0% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 27%.","The business throws off $94M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -5.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -3.1pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 29% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 70/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 41% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","29 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Head to Head Comparison: Mativ (NYSE:MATV) & Akzo Nobel (OTCMKTS:AKZOY)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/head-to-head-comparison-mativ-nysematv-akzo-nobel-otcmktsakzoy.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794611714.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"We Think You Should Be Aware Of Some Concerning Factors In Mativ Holdings' (NYSE:MATV) Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/ny